## 4 · 📏 SERVER-FIRST — the deploy rule

> **Develop and test on the SERVER. Push to GitHub only on an explicit order.**
> Flow: `server → local → GitHub`.

⚠️ **Why this is project-level and not universal:** it only matters in repos with auto-deploy.
**If your host deploys from `main`, any push to `main` is a production deploy.**

⬜ **Declare your repos below** — where the workshop lives, where the verified backup goes, where
the site publishes from. Delete the examples and put your own, or point at
the repos declared in `Mente/cuentas.tsv`. **Do not name a repo from memory.**

| Repo | Role |
|---|---|
| `github.com/<org>/<workshop-repo>` | ⭐ the **workshop's remote** — the server pushes here daily (`origin`) |
| `github.com/<org>/<product-repo>` | the **verified product's backup** (AGPL, GPG-signed by {{owner}}) (`backup`) |
| server `~/<workshop-dir>` | the workshop itself — **the source** |
| `<site-project>` | the site — **pushing to `main` publishes** |

